<c74object name="gst.orientation">
	<digest>
		Orientation and angles from IMU data stream [list]
	</digest>
	<description>
		<br/><o> gst.orientation </o> calculates orientation and angles from IMU data stream :
		<br/>raw accelerometer and raw gyroscope data stream.
		<br/>Uses <o> pipo.orientation </o>of MuBu package from ISMM team <br/>at IRCAM Centre Pompidou <a href="http://ismm.ircam.fr/pipo/">http://ismm.ircam.fr/pipo/</a>
		<br/><br/>The computation of the orientation is based on the fusion of <br/>the accelerometer and gyroscope data, using a complementory filter.
		<br/><br/>Our implementation was inspired from the ressources at IMU Guide: 
		<br/><a href="http://starlino.com/imu_guide.html">http://starlino.com/imu_guide.html</a>
		<br/><a href="http://www.starlino.com/imu_kalman_arduino.html">http://www.starlino.com/imu_kalman_arduino.html</a>
		<br/><br/>The code is similar to the implementation found here in javascript
		<br/><a href="https://github.com/ircam-ismm/como/blob/master/src/common/libs/lfo/Orientation.js">https://github.com/ircam-ismm/como/blob/master/src/common/libs/lfo/...</a>
		<br/><br/>The format for the riotbitalino and devicemotion can be found here: 
		<br/><a href="https://ircam-ismm.github.io/misc/riot-devicemotion-compatibility.html">https://ircam-ismm.github.io/misc/riot-devicemotion-compatibility.html</a>
		<br/><br/>The following document describes the computation for the angles
		<br/><a href="https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/application-note/AN3461.pdf">https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/application-note/AN3461.pdf</a>

	</description>
